  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>swarmchart3</keyword>
  <short_description>Display a 3-D swarm chart.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>swarmchart3(x, y, z)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>swarmchart3(x, y, z, sz, c)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>swarmchart3(..., propertyName, propertyValue)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>h = swarmchart3(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>swarmchart3</b> displays 3-D points using a scatter object. The returned object keeps the original <b>XData</b>, <b>YData</b>, and <b>ZData</b> and uses scatter jitter properties for the displayed x and y positions.</p>
    <p>Supported chart properties are <b>XJitter</b>, <b>XJitterWidth</b>, <b>YJitter</b>, <b>YJitterWidth</b>, and <b>ColorVariable</b>.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>Nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Display 3-D grouped observations.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data><![CDATA[swarmchart3([1 1 2 2], [1 2 1 2], [4 5 6 7], 40, [0 0.4 0.8], 'filled');]]></example_item_data>
      <example_item_img src="../../../../images/swarmchart3_1.svg" align="middle" generate="true" />
    </example_item>
  </examples>
  <see_also>
